25• There are three different types of arrays, and each value of the array 
is accessed using an ID, called the array index. 
-Indexed Array - An array with a digital index. Values are stored in linear 
fashions and accessed. 
- Associative array  − An array that contains strings as index. This stores 
values of elements not in a strict linear index order, but in association 
with key values. 
- Multidimensional array  − Access to an array containing one or more 
arrays and values using multiple indices .Types of Array 

